  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Supporting Justice Sector Reform &#x2013; Phase VII</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To advance institutional capacities of the Office of the Prosecutor General (OPG) in line with the International Humanitarian Law standards and organizational reform priorities. 2) To strengthen institutional and professional capacities of anti-corruption and law enforcement bodies. 3) To strengthen independence and improved efficiency of Ukraine&apos;s Judiciary and the Constitutional Court of Ukraine. 4) To increase transparency of the reform implementation. 5) To enhance capacity of public institutions to implement public sector, anti-corruption, governance and transparency and accountability reforms. 6) To enhance legal basis andstrategic foundations for criminal justice and public policy reform initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: OPG, National Anti-Corruption Bureau (NABU), Specialized Anti-corruption Prosecutor&#x2019;s Office (SAPO), Training Center of Prosecutors of Ukraine (TCPU), Bureau of Economic Security (BES), line ministries and agencies of the Government of Ukraine (GoU), Regional State Administrations and local self-governing bodies, anti-corruption civil society organizations.Indirect beneficiaries: Ukrainian population at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to advance the rule of law and public sector reforms in Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
